  "title": "Gao's theorem for nonabelian groups",
  "statement": {
    "representation": "markdown-latex",
    "text": "For every finite multiplicative group $G$, let $s(G)$ ( $s'(G)$ ) denote the smallest integer $m$ so that every sequence of $m$ elements of $G$ has a subsequence of length $>0$ (length $|G|$ ) which has product equal to 1 in some order.\n\nConjecture $s'(G) = s(G) + |G| - 1$ for every finite group $G$.",
